<Base title="Home" description="Cryptographic keys as atoms — public keys, key roles, succession chains, revocation records.">
  <h1>key-atoms</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 48rem;">
    Catalog <strong>#25</strong> of the <code>*-atoms</code> ecosystem and
    foundational for the v1.1.0 trust model. Public keys, key roles,
    succession chains, and revocation records published as atoms so every
    other catalog in the federation can verify signatures against a shared,
    versioned, content-addressed source of truth.
  </p>

  <h2>Bootstrap status</h2>
  <p>
    This catalog is in <code>lifecycle: bootstrap</code>. The ML-DSA-65 root
    key atom — the first content this catalog will hold — has not yet been
    published. Until that atom lands, no atom in the federation can be
    verified end-to-end.
  </p>

  <h2>Atom types</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>key</strong> — public-key record. Private key material is never published here.</li>
    <li><strong>revocation</strong> — key revocation record bound to a <code>key_id</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>succession</strong> — rotation chain linking a retired key to its successor.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Trust properties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Public-only</strong> — only public-key material is published. Private keys live offline.</li>
    <li><strong>Quantum-resistant</strong> — ML-DSA-65 is the Phase 1 baseline (NIST FIPS 204).</li>
    <li><strong>Role-based</strong> — signing roles (<code>root</code>, <code>editor</code>, <code>catalog-maintainer</code>, <code>ratifier</code>, <code>mirror-operator</code>) decouple authority from any individual key.</li>
    <li><strong>Rotatable</strong> — succession is an atom-publishing operation. Old keys remain immutable; <code>succeeded_by</code> is the only sanctioned post-publication mutation.</li>
    <li><strong>Verifiable</strong> — every atom in every dependent catalog references key atoms here by <code>signer_key_id</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="https://github.com/convergent-systems-co/atoms-spec">atoms-spec</a>,
    Part IV ("Signing and trust") for the full trust model.
  </p>
</Base>
